  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is being moved with a constant velocity under the action of an applied force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> along a frictionless surface with following surface profile.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0083_0550e5f0431d.png\" style=\"width: 221px; height: 138px;\" /></p><p>The correct applied force vs distance graph will be :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot1_0083_b80941c12e54.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 222px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot2_0083_5a645ec794cb.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 222px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0083_9390f958a208.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 222px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot4_0083_ef783924e6fb.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 216px;\" />",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When the block will be moving up the incline, the external force will be up the incline and will be balancing the down the incline component of gravity.</p><p>When the block will be moving down&nbsp;the incline, the external force will be again up the incline and will be balancing the down the incline component of gravity. But in this case the external force will be on the back side of the block.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>&#952;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0083_81df61dc3a99.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 216px;\" /></p>"
  }
}